course: dictionary
lesson: 15687
title: Timidity: shy, nervous and easily frightened
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Timidity means being shy, nervous or easily frightened. It is a lack of courage or confidence, so you hold back when something feels new or scary. The ending -ity turns the word timid, which describes a person, into timidity, which names the feeling.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Out of timidity, Mia hid behind her mum and did not say hello.» Mia did not say hello because she felt nervous. So timidity must mean shyness and fear of being noticed.
explain: Timidity is not a fault. Everyone feels shy sometimes, and a timid person can still be gentle, kind and brave. «She overcame her timidity and sang a solo at the concert.» To overcome something means to beat it or get past it.
fact: Timidity is a noun, so it names a quality: the state of being timid.
fact: «Timidity» means being shy, nervous or easily frightened.
fact: «Timidity» is uncountable, so you say «a lot of timidity», not «timidities».
fact: «Overcome your timidity» means become braver and get past feeling shy.
fact: Deer and rabbits often show timidity: they run away at the slightest sound.
exercise: «Out of timidity, Mia hid behind her mum.» Why did Mia hide? | She was playing a hiding game | She was too cold to stand up | *She felt shy and nervous | She was angry with her mum
exercise: What does «overcome your timidity» mean? | Grow taller than everyone else | Forget all your friends | Stop being brave | *Get past your shyness and become braver
exercise: Which animal often shows timidity? | *Rabbit | Crocodile | Lion | Tiger
test: Which word is closest in meaning to timidity? | Bravery | Strength | *Shyness | Anger
test: Is timidity a fault? | Only for grown-ups | *No, everyone feels shy sometimes | Only for animals | Yes, it is always a fault
exam: «The timidity of the young fawn made it hide in the long grass.» What does timidity mean here? | Being bold and fast | Being very tired | *Being shy and easily frightened | Being hungry
